§§ `s 1 "גיל הפרישה" for a person (lines 130-132)`

-- A man born 15 July 1950: Part A men, "May 1942 and after": 67 years, 804 months.
-- 804 months after 15 July 1950 is 15 July 2017.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age in months of` (`an Israeli employee` "Dov" `born` (YMD 1950 7 15) `who is` `male`) EQUALS 804
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Dov" `born` (YMD 1950 7 15) `who is` `male`) `on` (YMD 2017 7 14)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Dov" `born` (YMD 1950 7 15) `who is` `male`) `on` (YMD 2017 7 15)
-- A woman born 10 December 1955: "May 1947 to December 1955: 62" = 744 months; 744 months after
-- 10 December 1955 is 10 December 2017.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age in months of` (`an Israeli employee` "Edna" `born` (YMD 1955 12 10) `who is` `female`) EQUALS 744
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Edna" `born` (YMD 1955 12 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2017 12 9)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Edna" `born` (YMD 1955 12 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2017 12 10)
-- A woman born 10 January 1956: the Law's Part B, "May 1947 to December 1959: 62" = 744 months; 744 months after
-- 10 January 1956 is 10 January 2018.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age in months of` (`an Israeli employee` "Fay" `born` (YMD 1956 1 10) `who is` `female`) EQUALS 744
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Fay" `born` (YMD 1956 1 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2018 1 9)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Fay" `born` (YMD 1956 1 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2018 1 10)
-- A woman born 10 May 1964: 63 and 6 months = 762 months, reached 10 November 2027.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Hila" `born` (YMD 1964 5 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2027 11 9)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Hila" `born` (YMD 1964 5 10) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2027 11 10)
-- A woman born 20 June 1990: s 3, 65 years = 780 months, reached 20 June 2055.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age in months of` (`an Israeli employee` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female`) EQUALS 780
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2055 6 19)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female`) `on` (YMD 2055 6 20)
-- For a man, s 1 (1) sends to Part A of this Schedule; the Law's own age for a man born after April 1942 (s 3: 67) is the same.
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age in months of` (`an Israeli employee` "Gil" `born` (YMD 1959 3 1) `who is` `male`) EQUALS 804
-- A man born 1 March 1959 reaches 804 months on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Gil" `born` (YMD 1959 3 1) `who is` `male`) `on` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` (`an Israeli employee` "Gil" `born` (YMD 1959 3 1) `who is` `male`) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `The day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth (the ruling of 2026-10-08, SHRUG)`

-- Born 29 February 2008 (a leap year), 216 months (18 years) later: the year 2026 is not a leap year.
-- Clamped: 28 February 2026. Rolled: 1 March 2026. A day that exists is the same under every reading.
-- On 27 February 2026 neither reading has her at 18; on 1 March 2026 both do; on 28 February 2026 the
-- clamped reading has, the rolled has not: the default declines that one day.
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `reaches the age in months` 216 `, the last day of a shorter month` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `reaches the age in months` 216 `, the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT NOT `a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` (YMD 2026 2 27)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, reading` `age: the last day of the shorter month`
#ASSERT NOT `a person born on` (YMD 2008 2 29) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, reading` `age: the 1st of the next month`
-- Born 31 January 1990, 5 months (a test of the mechanism, not of any Part): reached 30 June 1990 or 1 July.
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 1990 1 31) `reaches the age in months` 5 `, the last day of a shorter month` EQUALS YMD 1990 6 30
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 1990 1 31) `reaches the age in months` 5 `, the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 1990 7 1
-- A day that exists: 15 March 1990 + 6 months is 15 September 1990, under every reading.
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 1990 3 15) `reaches the age in months` 6 `, the last day of a shorter month` EQUALS YMD 1990 9 15
#ASSERT `the day a person born on` (YMD 1990 3 15) `reaches the age in months` 6 `, the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 1990 9 15
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 1990 3 15) `has reached the age in months` 6 `on` (YMD 1990 9 15)
#ASSERT NOT `a person born on` (YMD 1990 3 15) `has reached the age in months` 6 `on` (YMD 1990 9 14)
